-- The people and businesses that were hardcoded in src/data/discover.ts, src/data/profile.ts,
-- src/data/booking.ts, src/data/market.ts and src/data/rentals.ts, as real, public profiles, so the
-- existing profile, business, studio, listing and review read code renders them from the database.
-- Same pattern as 20260913090949_seed_linked_profiles.sql and 20260914150000_import_profiles.sql:
-- each gets a sign-in-less auth.users row (no email, no password; nobody can sign in as them),
-- on_auth_user_created makes a bare profile, and the insert below fills it. Fixed uuids (uuid5 in the
-- import_profiles.py namespace, keyed "hardcoded:<file>:<id>").
--
--   profiles (+ auth.users)   17 rows: 10 talent, 7 business
--     talent    src/data/profile.ts Rahul Iyer; src/data/discover.ts Meher Kaur, DJ Noor, Arjun Menon,
--               Tanvi Rao, Zaid Qureshi, Lisa D'Souza, Harpreet Singh, Nithya Balan;
--               src/data/market.ts + rentals.ts Ravi Deshmukh (a person: talent, guitarist)
--     business  SoundHouse Studio, Swaraj Instruments, Pulse Live Systems (rentals.ts / market.ts);
--               Krimson Avenue (discover.ts); Headroom Mastering, The Basement Jam Rooms,
--               Waveform Podcast Studio (booking.ts). Business type is the first role; each has a
--               profile_business row (address = area and city, logo = the file's photo).
--   profile_role_details  9 rows   profile_services    4 rows (Rahul 3, Meher Kaur's
--   profile_experience    3 rows   profile_gallery     6 rows  mixing-and-mastering offer)
--   portfolio_items      13 rows   studios 4 rows, studio_rooms 4 rows, studio_equipment 3 rows
--   reviews               8 rows (Rahul Iyer 3, Ravi Deshmukh 2, Meher Kaur 1, SoundHouse Studio 1,
--                         Swaraj Instruments 1), name-only authors (author_profile_id null) as in the
--                         reviews already live
--   marketplace_listings  seller_profile_id set where seller_name is one of these five and no profile
--                         is linked yet (rows from 20260918220000_hardcoded_rows_to_db.sql)
--
-- Shapes are the ones the app reads: taxonomy slugs; "<role slug>:<label>" specialisations;
-- profiles.availability only where profile-view.ts maps it (Rahul: "Session Work"); the cards'
-- Available / Booked go to profile_role_details availability_status available_now / unavailable
-- (rendered "Available" / "Busy", as the hardcoded profile did) and to is_available; "Selective"
-- has no equivalent. Labels with no taxonomy slug are left out (genres Indie, Electronic, Ambient,
-- Pop Vocals, House, Techno, Desi Bass, Carnatic Fusion, Semi-Classical, Gully Rap, Folk,
-- Punjabi Folk; languages Sanskrit, Urdu, Konkani; instruments Synth, Bass, Percussion). City and
-- state are stored; the neighbourhood is kept only in business_address and studios.location.
-- No private field (email, phone, gender) is written. ananya.sharma (live QA account) is not touched.
--
-- Not stored, and why: counts the files showed (followers, ratings, review and rental totals,
-- credits, plays) were never counted from anything; studios.rating / review_count stay empty, as in
-- 20260918220000. The talent cards' per-song / per-show rates have no profile column (only an
-- hourly rate). Studio add-ons, non-hourly tiers, room descriptions, facilities with no amenity
-- slug, response times; Rahul's influences, other professional-detail rows, opportunity blurbs,
-- market entries (other sellers' listings), collaborators, mutuals and track durations; rental
-- review tags. market.ts review r3 (Aman Gill, "Rented backline") is the same review as rentals.ts
-- rv3 and is stored once. src/data/reviews.ts (the signed-in user's received and given reviews)
-- and bookings are the signed-in user's own activity and are left out.
--
-- Idempotent: fixed ids and ON CONFLICT; the listing update only fills an empty seller_profile_id.
--
-- Rollback (profiles, sections, studios, rooms, equipment and reviews cascade; listings' seller_profile_id
-- would cascade-delete the listings, so unlink them first):
--   UPDATE public.marketplace_listings SET seller_profile_id = NULL WHERE seller_profile_id IN (the ids in the DELETE below);
--   DELETE FROM auth.users WHERE id IN ('5a7466b9-2422-5d5d-9460-ee61b2002f13', '0662ace1-0642-5590-832f-f55fa23438f1', '61d15aab-b011-54ef-8644-b185711b608f', 'dbb4397e-9c0c-53d8-8624-2825c93d349f', '3fc0b746-3c09-5140-9270-549088a046db', 'e441dda1-4f3e-562a-812d-1a5525b9a90e', '0f820a59-9f0a-56a6-b1c4-99360bcc0d2c', '53147d82-58ac-5f17-97d3-f8125042e764', '689e3ab6-0309-58d2-9e9e-b7983d7dc132', '565f053c-eacc-50cb-854d-d5d2bc06b64e', '7d175f7d-88fd-5a16-ab64-48f852c60c7e', 'fc537d0d-0d31-5e6e-bc74-44d012f11f2d', '269fb1ae-0e54-53ef-8b67-b59865b14427', '4e4558aa-e260-5be1-a1db-ef48eaa6133d', '77423851-8af1-54e3-b5ab-bb449187d213', '79661e0a-7cb0-5696-b16b-478b56381277', '18128ebd-c739-5c2e-b041-55496fcb1771');

BEGIN;

